<h3 local-id=3D"4a16ad3a-14aa-4ff1-b339-036b3d13cd10" id=3D"DRPResourceUsag=
eEstimates-1.2.4.DataSelection">1.2.4. Data Selection</h3>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">select =
* from observations where
   observationStartMJD &lt;=3D (select min(observationStartMJD) from observ=
ations) + 365.25</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"2edab5b7-bd48-4c50-bdb8-5280d0aac727">This yields the first =
188340 visits from <code>baseline_v5.0.0_10yrs.db</code>.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"66969490-18e1-4403-9ba5-4c9c92bc04c8" id=3D"DRPResourceUsag=
eEstimates-1.3.Methodology">1.3. Methodology</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"834c5c33-c88a-4e2a-9d90-c6527b706dcf" id=3D"DRPResourceUsag=
eEstimates-1.3.1.Estimatingnumbersofquantapertask">1.3.1. Estimating number=
s of quanta per task</h3>
<h3 local-id=3D"e328cc41-8f8d-4a40-8130-bfba5e0294fb" id=3D"DRPResourceUsag=
eEstimates-1.3.2.Usingexistingresourceusagedatatopredictcputimeandmemoryreq=
uirements">1.3.2. Using existing resource usage data to predict cpu time an=
d memory requirements</h3>
<h2 local-id=3D"6c97e430-706f-4e94-b175-0a4bf7b27952" id=3D"DRPResourceUsag=
eEstimates-1.4.Wall-to-cputimeratios">1.4. Wall-to-cpu time ratios</h2>
<p local-id=3D"f42d8c78-e316-44fe-b2ab-727a0b8bcc5b">The estimates shown ab=
ove were derived using the per-job cpu time information in the task metadat=
a outputs. Some tasks can have a lot of I/O and that may dominate the wall =
time for those jobs. To get a sense of how prevalent those kinds of jobs ar=
e, I=E2=80=99ve extracted the distributions of wall-to-cpu time ratios for =
each of the tasks. The plot below shows the 0, 32, 50, 68, 100 percentile r=
anges of the wall-to-cpu time ratios for the tasks in DM-52645 (using w_202=
5_39), sorted by integrated wall time, in descending order.</p><span class=
